Tell the truth here. Do you add a circuit in the battery that says: 
If (time_elapsed>1 year) {
 (reduce_capacity(50%))
}
?

@jeevs Great, I'll totally support folks who want to move into TPM. It's vital that we understand why folks want to move TO TPM instead of AWAY from whatever they're currently doing, as you pointed out. It sounds like your rationale to reach that conclusion is sound based on what you've written above. 

You asked for my personal take on keeping work meaningful in TPM roles. For me, it's about trying to find something personally interesting or different in what I'm working on. For example, I'm very much drinking the Kool-Aid with the mission of both my current company and last company (Upstart - Continue using AI to provide non-predatory credit to all, Twitch - Build cutting edge video streaming technology to enable a creator/viewer ecosystem that didn't exist before)

Even more personally, I'm not in "climb the career ladder ASAP" mode anymore because I have a 2 year old and a 2 month old. I picked my current role because it's 100% remote first and I'm trying to find the balance between being a father/husband vs a TPM. My priority is definitely to be a father who happens to be a TPM instead of the other way around. With that in mind, it's fine for me to deal with familiar challenges at work.
